) correctly handles extreme positive values without overflow or modification.'}, {'input': [], 'expected': 'If the delegate returns a negative zero (e.g., ConstantIndicator(-0.0)), NumericIndicator.abs().getValue(0) should be 0.0 (positive zero), confirming correct handling of signed zero.', 'description': 'Check that abs() normalises negative zero to standard zero.'}, {'input': [], 'expected': 'For a delegate that yields NaN (e.g., ConstantIndicator(Num.NaN)), NumericIndicator.abs().getValue(0) should also be NaN, preserving the undefined nature of the value.', 'description': 'Ensure that abs() propagates NaN values unchanged.'}, {'input': [], 'expected': 'The NumericIndicator returned by abs() must retain the same BarSeries as the original indicator; calling getBarSeries() on both instances should return the identical BarSeries object.', 'description': 'Confirm that the series context is preserved after applying abs().'}, {'input': [], 'expected': 'The delegate of the indicator returned by abs() must be a different object from the original delegate (i.e., NumericIndicator.abs().delegate() != original.delegate()), while still producing identical absolute values for all indices.', 'description': 'Verify that abs() creates a new delegate wrapper rather than reusing the original, ensuring immutability of the delegate chain.'}]}]
